        <h2>Mahanubhav Panth: An Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            <span>Sri Gopal Krishna Maharaj ki Jai</span>
            <span>Sri Dattatreya Maharaj ki Jai</span>
            <span>Sri Chakrapani Maharaj ki Jai</span>
            <span>Sri Govind Prabhu Maharaj ki Jai</span>
            <span>Sarvagya Sri Chakradhar Swami ki Jai</span>
        </p>
        <p>Mahanubhav Panth is a religious sect which follows the teachings of Srimad Bhagvad Gita and Sri Brahmvidya Shastra. Established around 800 years ago by Sarvagy Sri Chakradhar Swamiji in Maharashtra, this sect believes in single-minded devotion (“ananya bhakti”) of the Almighty God and its five incarnations (“panch avatars”). </p>
        <p>The five avatars we are firmly devoted to are: Lord Sri Krishna, Bhagvan Sri Dattatreya Maharaj, Sri Chakrapani Prabhu Maharaj, Sri Govind Prabhu Maharaj and Sarvagy Sri Chakradhar Swami ji. This means that Mahanubhav Panth believes in the Theory of Incarnation (“avatarvad”).</p>
        <p>The Supreme God took these five incarnations for the sole purpose of giving Godly knowledge (“Gyan”)and Godly Love (“Prem”) to the deserving human beings (Adhikari jeev) so that they can get rid of the cycle of life and death and attain Moksha (or Parmanand). From this position, soul never returns back to this earth again. So, we believe these two be the main sources of imancipation. </p>
        <p>As per their teachings, Mahanubhav Panth believes in duality (“dvaitvad”) of Atma and Parmatma. This is based on our principal belief that there are four original, independent and indestructible elements (“char padarths”) namely jeev (soul), devta (deities), prapanch (five materials namely earth, water, air, fire and ether) and God. God is Supreme and only He has the power of creation, maintenance and destruction of this universe. All others gods, from Chaitanya Maya down to Karmabhumi devtas, follow His command. </p>
        <p>We also believe in four other “means” which can take us nearer to our sole goal of moksha. They are, “sthan, prasad, vaasnik and bhikshuks.” We hold all the four with extreme reverence and all the four are part of our daily puja-avsars. </p>
        <p>Mahanubhav Panth believes in the Principle of Karma as enunciated by Lord Sri Krishna and clearly understands that by following it, we can try to escape from faulty karmas or sins and focus only on noble karmas. </p>
        <p>Any one who wants to get initiated into the sect has to first understand the basic principles of the sect and take a vow of abstaining from non-vegetarianism, alcohol, gambling, stealing and committing to good character and truthfulness. Then one join the sect by taking ‘naam’ (guru-mantra) from some panthic saint of one’s choice. After that, the disciple must do puja-vandan two/three times a day in the way as explained by ones guru and offer bhog to God daily. </p>
        <p>It is very clear that Mahanubhav Panth believes in the worship of Supreme God alone and ‘not’ in the worship of any god/deity. We firmly believe that only by following the teachings of Lord Sri Krishna and Sarvagya Sri Chakradhar Swami, we can attain the goal of human existence.</p>
